{"chunk_id":"R2-2311262-001","collection":"ran2_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Ericsson"],"tdocNumber":"R2-2311262","title":"Advices for WI CR writing"},"point_id":"7737117271976130369"}
After November RAN, the Rel-18 WI CRs will be merged and form the first rel-18 3x.331 versions v18.0.0 This document provides some guidelines and recommentations on how to achieve top-quality WI CRs. On Track Changes: Ensure there is no changes on changes. Do not use colored text. Use single tracking user for a "contiguous change" (such that simple "select/copy/paste" can be used when implementing CR to the spec. E.g., if you add a new section, a new paragragh, a new sentence, a new field descr, or some other item, they should be introduced with s single tracking user, to make select-copy-paste simpler and faster (double-klikck. New paragraphs, sentences and even words where multiple tracking users have contributed to the colourful text requires the merger to be more accurate when selecting text to copy/paste. Avoid e.g. Ensure the ASN.1 is correct (passes syntax checking, finds naming mistakes, May include complete ASN.1 in the WI CR. Use ENUMERATED {ffs} when the structure of a field (e.g. a SEQUENCE) is not ready. Use maxFFS as upper limit, e.g. INTEGER(1..maxFFS), SIZE{1..maxFFS}. IMPORT of field/IEs from other RRC module Use correct Word styles (see RRC Handbook [1] on how to create CR and check styles in the CR). Respect the RRC style (procedure layout, section layout, naming rules, extension rules, Need Codes…). RRC Rapp proposes the recommendations listed in previous section are respected during the work with Rel-18 WI CR completion.

