After Dec versions of TS 36.331 and TS 38.331 are published, the WI running CR Rapporteurs will port the running CRs to the new specification, that is create new running CRs with the new spec as baseline. When porting a running CR to the new specification, it is recommended that the complete specification is kept within the CR (i.e., unchanged parts/sections are not deleted). Then, the overall specification impact of the new Rel-16 feature is easier visualized, and specification quality is easier ensured (e.g. new sections, field and IE names). Unchanged parts of the running CR can be deleted as a late CR Rapporteur activity before CR agreement. It is also recommended that draft running CRs are stored on ftp server, and not circulated in mails on the reflector. ftp://ftp.3gpp.org/Email_Discussions/RAN2

